      "id": "claim_263785b45ee9494c98b6f642ae502eb3",
      "statement": "src/features/organizer/externalApi.ts publishes the plugin-to-plugin interface as Zotero.FlexAnnotate with a versioned, stable contract: EXTERNAL_API_VERSION (bumped on breaking changes), EXTERNAL_NAMESPACE \"FlexAnnotate\", pluginID (the configured addon id), getHeadings (flat headings with id/title/num/path/depth/tag) and getOutline (raw { roots } tree), each accepting (libraryID, collectionKey?) where a top-level collection key picks a collection tree and null picks the library tree.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/features/organizer/externalApi.ts#L14-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dec9082a246e637d03a48e531578d27f0598a68c1192109f970cb5a6690a9be2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2064a1ced99b4745ad79f00b9240a215",
      "statement": "The external API is installed on the shared Zotero namespace at feature start and removed at feature stop via the externalApi feature in hooks.ts, so the namespace never leaks after shutdown; installExternalApi is idempotent and never clobbers a namespace owned by a different plugin (the conflict is logged via Zotero.logError instead), and uninstallExternalApi deletes the namespace only when the installed pluginID is its own.",
      "evidence": [
