      "statement": "Failure semantics and teardown of the persistent dialog: openPersistent failing before a window exists falls back to the native dialog path, failing after the window opened never opens a second dialog on the same io, a single window close without accept resolves the pending request promise Zotero waits on; stop() restores all three patched methods, flushes the rect pref, drops pendingInsert/lastCommand and closes the browse window; turning the option off closes nothing immediately (the window stays until the next insert, which does not reopen it), and turning it on mid-dialog arms the running window via activatePersistentOnOpenDialog.",
